  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>We know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mo>&#183;</mo></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;represents the greatest integer function.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>But&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Not possible because we know that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and also, we know that if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>And,&nbsp;now&nbsp;by using the definition of logarithm, we have,&nbsp;if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
